The announced primary returned HTTP 521, and the documented integration
endpoint did not serve this pin. The Codeberg mirror was used under the
fallback rule. Its pin is one mirror-specific setup.sh fix ahead of the
documented integration endpoint tip d8aafb76eeef070dad2dc39161ddf922545fce90.
The old SukiSU-Ultra history and this branch share the cf41f112 ancestor, then
diverge; the old branch tip is not an ancestor of builtin-new.

Local compatibility patches: builtin-new-kernel-5.10-compat.patch,
builtin-new-build-version.patch, and builtin-new-susfs-v2.3-compat.patch.
The Linux 5.10 SUSFS pathname hook ABI is adapted by
scripts/apply-sukisu-susfs-5.10-path-abi.py.
The local SUSFS v2.3.0 core uses the legacy SELinux backup-policy query path;
builtin-new's v2.4 native SELinux table calls are gated until that API exists.
The optional priority UID filter is disabled because the local core does not
expose its command/API.
